Freedom: refuse the local host for connections from user inbounds

FORK DEVIATION: not upstream code. Upstream's freedom (310b764, 4e87f59, d52f150, 958eb9e and
63ca2e0, in v26.11.9) blocks private destinations after resolution for the vless, vmess, trojan,
shadowsocks, hysteria, wireguard and masque inbounds through finalRules, built on common/geodata
from the geodata refactor 82624bc, which the pin does not have. This patch keeps only what the node needs: a
connection whose inbound is vless, vmess, trojan, hysteria, wireguard or any shadowsocks inbound,
the names those inbounds set in session.Inbound at the pin, may not reach a loopback address
(127.0.0.0/8, ::1 and IPv4-mapped loopback) or an unspecified one (0.0.0.0, ::), which is never
a remote destination. Private ranges, 100.64.0.0/10 and link-local stay reachable, and
dokodemo-door, socks and http inbounds are not affected.

Freedom refuses a literal or freedom-resolved destination before it dials, and after it dials it
closes, before any payload, a connection whose remote end is loopback, which covers a domain the
system resolver or sockopt resolved. A connection made through sockopt.dialerProxy reports
0.0.0.0:0 as its remote end, so the after-dial check reads only loopback. UDP packets that a user
inbound addresses per packet are dropped when their resolved address is the local host.
proxy/freedom/local_host_refusal_test.go is fork code.

